<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The fractal marker for the drone-in-a-box landing surface.

  WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE MODEL AND NOT PART OF box.xacro
  The obvious approach -- put the <visual> inside <gazebo reference="base_link">
  in box.xacro -- LOOKS right and fails silently. sdformat's URDF parser does
  not keep such a block as its own visual: it strips the <visual> wrapper and
  merges the children into the link's EXISTING visual, producing

      <visual name='base_link_visual'>
        <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry><mesh><uri>...BOX PAD1.0_simple.dae</uri></mesh></geometry>
        <pose>0.0129 -0.1456 0.5896 -1.5708 0 0</pose>   <- second <pose>
        <geometry><plane>...</plane></geometry>          <- second <geometry>

  A visual may only have one <pose> and one <geometry>; the first wins, so the
  plane is dropped with no error and no warning. Verified by diffing the xacro
  output against `gz sdf -p`: the URDF contains landing_marker_visual once, the
  converted SDF contains it zero times. URDF also has no <plane> geometry and
  no PBR albedo_map of its own, so there is no way to express this marker in
  URDF at all -- hence a real SDF model, spawned separately.

  SIZE. The plane is 0.6241 m, not 0.50 m. marker.png carries a white quiet
  zone (1 module of a 5-level fractal => the black marker is 0.8012 of the
  image side). 0.6241 * 0.8012 = 0.5000, so the BLACK marker measures exactly
  the 0.50 m that offboard_precland_params.yaml's marker_size declares. Change
  one of those two numbers and you must change the other.

  NO COLLISION on purpose. The box's own mesh already provides the landing
  surface; a second collider sitting 1 cm above it would make the drone touch
  down on the marker instead of the box floor and could trip the land detector
  early.
-->
<sdf version="1.9">
  <model name="dib_box_marker">
    <static>true</static>
    <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
    <link name="base">
      <visual name="marker_visual">
        <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <plane>
            <normal>0 0 1</normal>
            <size>0.6241 0.6241</size>
          </plane>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <diffuse>1 1 1 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>
          <pbr>
            <metal>
              <albedo_map>model://fractal_aruco_marker/marker.png</albedo_map>
            </metal>
          </pbr>
        </material>
      </visual>
    </link>
  </model>
</sdf>
